From: Husarion <support@husarion.com>
Subject: [PATCH] SHM: only one process resets a port mutex whose owner died

A port's named mutex (<domain>_port<N>_mutex, a POSIX semaphore) serializes
every open, regeneration and removal of the port's segment. When its owner
dies holding it (a participant SIGKILLed inside open_port_internal, which
holds it through healthy_check), every process that then needs the port waits
2 s, removes the name, creates a mutex of its own and locks it. A port
regeneration makes every participant on the host wait at once, so they time
out within the same second, each holds a different mutex, and
open_port_internal runs in several processes at the same time: one removes
the segment another has just created, and the discovery port ends as several
segments, each still marked ok, with listeners stranded on the unlinked ones.
Participants on different segments no longer hear each other's announcements
and a newcomer sees only part of the world, until every process restarts.

The port paths now take the mutex through *_robust_named_mutex(): every
holder first holds a kernel flock on the file <domain>_port<N>_mutex_holder in
the lock directory, released right after the mutex. The kernel releases it
when its holder dies, so the process that times out on the mutex holds the
file lock and is the only one resetting the mutex; the others wait for the
file lock (up to 10 s for a live holder, then fail as before). The file is
never removed. A process without this patch does not take the file lock and
behaves as before. The ABI does not change (private headers only).

---
--- a/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemGlobal.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/rtps/transport/shared_mem/SharedMemGlobal.hpp
@@ -481,7 +481,7 @@
                     if (node_->is_port_ok)
                     {
                         deleted_unique_ptr<SharedMemSegment::named_mutex> port_mutex =
-                                SharedMemSegment::try_open_and_lock_named_mutex(segment_name + "_mutex");
+                                SharedMemSegment::try_open_and_lock_robust_named_mutex(segment_name + "_mutex");
 
                         std::unique_lock<SharedMemSegment::named_mutex> port_lock(*port_mutex, std::adopt_lock);
 
@@ -1056,7 +1056,7 @@
                                                        << port_segment_name);
 
         deleted_unique_ptr<SharedMemSegment::named_mutex> port_mutex =
-                SharedMemSegment::open_or_create_and_lock_named_mutex(port_segment_name + "_mutex");
+                SharedMemSegment::open_or_create_and_lock_robust_named_mutex(port_segment_name + "_mutex");
 
         std::unique_lock<SharedMemSegment::named_mutex> port_lock(*port_mutex, std::adopt_lock);
 
--- a/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/SharedMemSegment.hpp
+++ b/src/cpp/utils/shared_memory/SharedMemSegment.hpp
@@ -40,7 +40,19 @@
 #include <boost/interprocess/offset_ptr.hpp>
 #include <boost/thread/thread_time.hpp>
 
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cstring>
+#include <thread>
+
+#if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(MINGW_COMPILER)
+#include <fcntl.h>
+#include <sys/file.h>
+#include <sys/stat.h>
+#include <unistd.h>
+#endif // if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(MINGW_COMPILER)
+
 #include "BoostAtExitRegistry.hpp"
+#include "SharedDir.hpp"
 #include "RobustInterprocessCondition.hpp"
 #include "SharedMemUUID.hpp"
 
@@ -180,6 +192,139 @@
         return named_mutex;
     }
 
+    /**
+     * open_or_create_and_lock_named_mutex() for a mutex whose owner may die
+     * holding it (a shared-memory port's mutex): every holder first holds a
+     * kernel lock on a file of its own (HolderFile), released right after the
+     * mutex. The kernel drops that lock when its holder dies, so the process that
+     * times out on the named mutex knows its owner is dead (or is a process
+     * without this lock) and is the only one removing and recreating it. Without
+     * the file lock, every process that waits on a dead owner's mutex times out
+     * on its own, removes the name and locks a fresh mutex of its own, and
+     * several processes then open, remove and create the same port at once.
+     */
+    static deleted_unique_ptr<SharedSegmentBase::named_mutex> open_or_create_and_lock_robust_named_mutex(
+            const std::string& mutex_name)
+    {
+        HolderFile holder(mutex_name, BOOST_INTERPROCESS_TIMEOUT_WHEN_LOCKING_DURATION_MS * 10);
+        return holder.attach(open_or_create_and_lock_named_mutex(mutex_name));
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * try_open_and_lock_named_mutex() under the same file lock as
+     * open_or_create_and_lock_robust_named_mutex().
+     */
+    static deleted_unique_ptr<SharedSegmentBase::named_mutex> try_open_and_lock_robust_named_mutex(
+            const std::string& mutex_name)
+    {
+        HolderFile holder(mutex_name, BOOST_INTERPROCESS_TIMEOUT_WHEN_LOCKING_DURATION_MS * 2);
+        return holder.attach(try_open_and_lock_named_mutex(mutex_name));
+    }
+
+    /**
+     * A kernel lock (flock) on the file <mutex name>_holder in the lock
+     * directory. Waits up to timeout_ms for a live holder and throws after that:
+     * it never takes the lock from a live holder. The file is never removed.
+     */
+    class HolderFile
+    {
+    public:
+
+        HolderFile(
+                const std::string& mutex_name,
+                uint32_t timeout_ms)
+        {
+#if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(MINGW_COMPILER)
+            const std::string path = SharedDir::get_lock_path(mutex_name + "_holder");
+            auto deadline = std::chrono::steady_clock::now() + std::chrono::milliseconds(timeout_ms);
+            while (true)
+            {
+                // Open an existing file without O_CREAT: in a sticky shared directory
+                // (/dev/shm) the kernel refuses O_CREAT on a file another user owns
+                // (fs.protected_regular), whatever the capabilities, and processes of
+                // several users share one port.
+                fd_ = ::open(path.c_str(), O_RDONLY | O_CLOEXEC);
+                if (fd_ == -1 && errno == ENOENT)
+                {
+                    fd_ = ::open(path.c_str(), O_RDONLY | O_CREAT | O_EXCL | O_CLOEXEC, 0666);
+                    if (fd_ == -1 && errno == EEXIST)
+                    {
+                        continue; // created by another process meanwhile: open that one
+                    }
+                }
+                if (fd_ == -1)
+                {
+                    throw std::runtime_error("Couldn't open " + path + ": " + std::strerror(errno));
+                }
+                if (0 == ::flock(fd_, LOCK_EX | LOCK_NB))
+                {
+                    // The lock counts only on the file the name points to now.
+                    struct stat locked = {};
+                    struct stat named = {};
+                    if (0 == ::fstat(fd_, &locked) && 0 == ::stat(path.c_str(), &named) &&
+                            locked.st_ino == named.st_ino && locked.st_dev == named.st_dev)
+                    {
+                        return;
+                    }
+                }
+                ::close(fd_);
+                fd_ = -1;
+                if (std::chrono::steady_clock::now() >= deadline)
+                {
+                    throw std::runtime_error("Couldn't lock " + path + ": held by a live process");
+                }
+                std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(5));
+            }
+#else
+            (void)mutex_name;
+            (void)timeout_ms;
+#endif // if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(MINGW_COMPILER)
+        }
+
+        ~HolderFile()
+        {
+            release(fd_);
+        }
+
+        /**
+         * Hands the file lock to the returned pointer, which releases it right
+         * after the named mutex object is destroyed.
+         */
+        template<class NamedMutexPtr>
+        deleted_unique_ptr<SharedSegmentBase::named_mutex> attach(
+                NamedMutexPtr&& named_mutex)
+        {
+            auto deleter = named_mutex.get_deleter();
+            int fd = fd_;
+            fd_ = -1;
+            return deleted_unique_ptr<SharedSegmentBase::named_mutex>(
+                named_mutex.release(),
+                [fd, deleter](SharedSegmentBase::named_mutex* p)
+                {
+                    deleter(p);
+                    release(fd);
+                });
+        }
+
+    private:
+
+        static void release(
+                int fd)
+        {
+#if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(MINGW_COMPILER)
+            if (fd != -1)
+            {
+                ::flock(fd, LOCK_UN);
+                ::close(fd);
+            }
+#else
+            (void)fd;
+#endif // if !defined(_MSC_VER) && !defined(MINGW_COMPILER)
+        }
+
+        int fd_ = -1;
+    };
+
     static deleted_unique_ptr<SharedSegmentBase::named_mutex> open_or_create_named_mutex(
             const std::string& mutex_name)
     {
